  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The following video will help you understand exactly what kind of strange movement you are looking for.\nhttps://youtu.be/3-e0Mybq8Zo\nAs a detail, some avatars that have their own movement animations set in the Base layer, when moving in desktop mode or with 3-point tracking, somehow bend at the waist when they stop moving, as shown in the video.\nThis does not happen in the Live version.\nAll Tracking Controls are set to Tracking and Use Auto-Footsteps for 3 and 4 point tracking is turned off. (This is because it behaves strangely when Use Auto-Footsteps is turned on. (This is probably due to conflicting movement animations and may be a specification, but we will report it separately if necessary.)\nThe Base layer is almost the same as the original, except that some of the animation files in the Locomotion layer included in the VRCSDK have been replaced and some settings in the Animator Tracking Control have been changed. Upon closer examination, it seems that the bug occurs when the BlendTree animation set to Standing in the Locomotion layer meets certain conditions.\nAgain, this bug does not occur in the Live version. It seems to be a bug that occurred with the new IK.",
